From aea3fa872a07fd224f9b31ca0a42393af29e9da2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FreeKC <fredrenaud25@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 06:33:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] chore(ci): make format, lint, typecheck and tests pass on
 main

`deno fmt --check` failed on the bundled Font Awesome SVGs under
`public/fonts`, which are vendored assets rather than source, so they are
excluded from formatting like `assets/` already is. The three `.vscode`
files are reformatted in place.

`deno lint` failed on two imports `index.ts` stopped using when reconcile
moved to the `derive_group_state` RPC (#39). The same change left the
orchestration suite without a stub for that RPC, and the skip path now
records the observed chain tip (#44), so three tests failed on main. The
stub answers `rpc()` with no rows and records the call, and the skip test
expects the one checkpoint update that path performs.

The workflow ran `deno test --allow-env tests/`, which cannot read the
PGlite data files that the derive_group_state and ledger lag suites load,
so both suites failed on every run. It now runs `deno task test`, the
command CONTRIBUTING.md documents, which grants the read and network
permissions those suites need.
